<details><summary>Reproducer (text watcher, at 03a253c2)</summary>

Chromium's "Copy image" writes `image/png` and, when the image has a URL, also `text/html` `<img>` markup (`SystemClipboard::WriteImageWithTag`, `third_party/blink/renderer/core/clipboard/system_clipboard.cc`, lines 301-347). `wl-paste --type text` falls back to any `text/*` type when no `text/plain` is offered (`src/wl-paste.c`, lines 145-148, wl-clipboard 2.3.0). Its bookmark write also adds `text/x-moz-url` (`clipboard_ozone.cc`, lines 746-754; Chromium main 9d90aa5c). `source.c` is a clipboard owner with these three types that serves every read separately, as Chromium's Wayland data source does. Only the text watcher from `Clipboard.qml` at the PR head is running.

The text watcher reads `text/html` from the image owner on the copy and stores the markup as a text entry. A later image paste is still identical.

